eatures/F0032-knowledge-evolution-engine/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0041 \u2014 Learning Plane](features/F0041-learning-plane/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0042 \u2014 Knowledge promotion/governance](features/F0042-knowledge-promotion-and-governance/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0043 \u2014 Generalized review queues / governance](features/F0043-generalized-review-queues-and-governance/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0067 \u2014 Graph Observatory](features/F0067-graph-observatory/README.md) - Planned (added 2026-10-13, ADR-0071/ADR-0072)\n\n**v0.3 (Later)**\n\n- [F0048 \u2014 Process domain model](features/F0048-process-domain-model/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0049 \u2014 Canonical Transition Service](features/F0049-canonical-transition-service/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0050 \u2014 Temporal.io](features/F0050-temporal-io/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0051 \u2014 Process Workbench](features/F0051-process-workbench/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0052 \u2014 Normative constraints](features/F0052-normative-constraints/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0053 \u2014 Hypothetical scenarios](features/F0053-hypothetical-scenarios/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0054 \u2014 Process reconciliation](features/F0054-process-reconciliation/README.md) - Planned\n\n**v0.4+ (Later)**\n\n- [F0055 \u2014 Native reasoning](features/F0055-native-reasoning/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0056 \u2014 Derived dependency invalidation](features/F0056-derived-dependency-invalidation/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0057 \u2014 Decision ledger](features/F0057-decision-ledger/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0058 \u2014 Historical decision replay](features/F0058-historical-decision-replay/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0059 \u2014 Execution gate](features/F0059-execution-gate/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0060 \u2014 Reasoning-pattern governance](features/F0060-reasoning-pattern-governance/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0061 \u2014 Advanced retrieval](features/F0061-advanced-retrieval/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0062 \u2014 Advanced reasoners](features/F0062-advanced-reasoners/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0063 \u2014 Future DSL](features/F0063-future-dsl/README.md) - Planned\n- [F0068 \u2014 Spectral graph retrieval experiments](features/F0068-spectral-graph-retrieval-experiments/README.md) - Planned; conditional v0.4+, after baseline measurement\n\n### 3.4 MVP User Stories\n\nAuthored per feature in `features/F####-{slug}/F####-S####-{slug}.md`. The v0.1 acceptance questions in sections 86 and 87 are the minimum story set for F0024 and F0025. F0001 carries seven stories: toolchain skeleton, local containers and dependency matrix, the four section 115.4 proofs, and contract settlement (see section 3.3).\n\n### 3.4.1 Examples as acceptance artifacts\n\nEvery new or changed semantic concept needs a definition, worked example, boundary case, and owning feature/story/contract links. Start with [EX-GL-001](examples/neurosymbolic-gl/README.md) and the [coverage map](examples/README.md). Structured examples validate against declared local schemas; runtime stories must later reproduce observed outcomes. Synthetic examples, observed proof evidence, and independent frozen evaluation data remain explicitly distinguished. F0065 carries six unstarted stories; its drafted examples do not constitute runtime delivery.\n\n### 3.5 Screen Specifications\n\nMinimal Entity 360 and Document 360 (sections 70, 71) and the constrained chat surface (section 72) are the v0.1 screens; specs land in `screens/` during Phase A of their features. F0065 S0005 extends Entity 360 with the bounded guideline assessment panel specified in its PRD; it introduces no standalone workbench.\n\n---\n\n## 4) Phase B \u2014 Architect Spec\n\nStatus: the architecture baseline exists in the master blueprint; each subsection below summarizes it and points to the authoritative sections. Per-feature Phase B produces assembly plans, contract files, and ADR confirmations.\n\nOntology prerequisite amendment: read the [planning handoff](architecture/ontology-planning-handoff.md) before planning F0012/F0013/F0015. It records release identities, constraint execution, missingness, dependency links, and deferred F0030/F0062 work. The six affected features have planning-only KG mappings so lookup exposes their context; PRDs, stories, assembly plans and Phase A/B approvals remain pending, and ADR-0045 stays Proposed.\n\n### 4.1 Service Boundaries\n\nEight architectural planes (section 4) implemented as a modular monolith across `engine/` (semantic kernel, commit services, governance, review, search, security), `neuron/` (interpretation, conversation, learning, agent tools), and `experience/` (native semantic UX, including the Review Panel), with Docling, the direct-baseline vLLM client, PostgreSQL extensions, and (from v0.3) Temporal as engines around the semantic core (ADR-0001 as amended by ADR-0057, sections 100 and 125; Docling-Graph was rejected with ADR-0060 on 2026-11-08, section 126). Engine packages as built through F0008 are listed in master blueprint section 77; the container topology is unchanged (`architecture/c4-container.md`). The deployable topology and dependency matrix are a P0 pre-build requirement (section 106.2).\n\n### 4.2 Data Model\n\nPostgreSQL is authoritative (ADR-0002). Kernel entities: Tenant, Workspace, KnowledgeBase, Principal, SourceDocument, DocumentVersion, ContentArtifact, ContentBlock, DocumentProfile, ExtractionProfile, SemanticInterpretationRun, Assertion, Entity, FactSlot, CanonicalFactVersion, CanonicalRelationshipVersion (a logical name: RELATIONSHIP FactSlot versions live in `canonical_fact_version`, ADR-0078), Derivation, ReviewItem, ReviewDecision, LearningCandidate, Conversation, AuditEvent, OutboxEvent (definitions in `domain/glossary.md`). Core tables are listed in section 78 and mirrored in `architecture/data-model.md`; AGE labels in section 79; content artifact layout in sections 80 and 81. Every authoritative row carries `tenant_id`, `knowledge_base_id`, and audit fields (`created_at`, `recorded_at`, actor). FactSlot identity (section 13; ADR-0077), bitemporal fact versions (section 14; ADR-0078), and change semantics (section 16) define canonical truth. Deployed schema (migrations 0001\u20130015) is mapped table by table in master blueprint section 78; F0009 adds migration 0016 (two append-only lineage tables and review-decision guards, section 4.18). F0012 adds migration 0017 (eight append-only ontology release tables and the `ontology_release` access type, section 4.19).\n\n### 4.3 Workflow Rules\n\nIngestion and interpretation (section 86), the human review round trip (section 75), endorsement supersession (section 87), and knowledge promotion (section 42) are the baseline workflows; every state transition is an append-only canonical commit or review decision. Process semantics and Temporal execution are v0.3 (sections 59 to 62, ADR-0028).\n\n### 4.4 Authorization Model\n\nVerified `(issuer, subject)` mapped to a stable internal principal; typed resource and action policies evaluated through a native Casbin adapter; tenant and knowledge-base membership resolved separately from resource scope; enforcement at API, commit, search, vector, graph, evidence, ontology, conversation context, MCP, and execution gate; user, service, and agent principals distinct with bounded delegation; every authorization decision audited with policy version (sections 66, 118 to 120; ADR-0049/ADR-0050 accepted for the F0001-S0006 boundary and ADR-0061/ADR-0062 for the F0002 scope; ADR-0051 to ADR-0053 Proposed).\n\n### 4.5 API Contracts\n\nSemantic REST API surface in section 68 (`GET` and `POST` over `/entities`, `/assertions`, `/facts`, `/relationships`, `/documents`, `/content`, `/ontology`, `/search`, `/graph`, `/evidence`, `/history`, `/conversations`, `/learning`, `/reviews`), and read-first MCP tools in section 69. OpenAPI lives in `api/brain-api.yaml` and is authored per feature.\n\n### 4.6 Non-Functional Requirements\n\nPerformance, availability, scalability, and security targets are proposed gates in sections 114.2 and 115.2 and require baseline measurement and named owners before acceptance: extraction reuse with zero re-parse, evidence fidelity for every citation, temporal integrity under concurrent commits, zero unauthorized content in the isolation suite, ingestion recovery without duplicate effects, timed restore drills, and measured field precision and recall, latency, and cost on the frozen slice. Latency budgets are expressed in milliseconds per surface once measured.\n\n### 4.7 Architecture Artifacts\n\n- `architecture/master-blueprint.md` \u2014 full baseline\n- `architecture/decisions/` \u2014 ADR-0001 to ADR-0079 (master blueprint section 76 carries the reconciled status register; Accepted architecture and Proposed contracts; ADR-0060 (Docling-Graph) was Rejected on 2026-11-08; ADR-0038/0039/0042/0043/0051/0052/0053 have operator decisions recorded (2026-11-08) and stay Proposed until proven; ADR-0063 is accepted as direction and ADR-0064 to ADR-0069 are Proposed, section 4.11; ADR-0070 proposes the account, party and role model, section 4.8; ADR-0071 and ADR-0072 propose the semantic execution trace contract and the read-only Graph Observatory boundary, see `architecture/graph-observatory-design.md`; ADR-0077 is Accepted (F0007); ADR-0078 (the F0008 bitemporal version contract) is Accepted (2026-11-19), section 4.15; ADR-0073 (F0004) and ADR-0075 (F0006) remain Proposed after their features closed, pending the proof gates named in each record; ADR-0079 (F0011 offline schema bundle) is Proposed with its acceptance proofs met in feature run 2026-11-22-885e8734, pending operator acceptance, section 4.16)\n- `architecture/data-model.md` \u2014 tables, graph labels, artifact layout\n- `architecture/SOLUTION-PATTERNS.md` \u2014 project conventions (seeded at F0001 Phase B)\n- `architecture/c4-context.md`, `architecture/c4-container.md` \u2014 C4 L1 and L2 (Mermaid; ASCII companion in ADR-0054)\n- `api/brain-api.yaml` \u2014 OpenAPI 3.1 (F0001 scope: health, protected reads, webhook, commit)\n- `schemas/*.schema.json` \u2014 shared JSON Schemas (manifest, interpretation result, review decision, commit request and response, problem details); `semantic-example.schema.json` and `commercial-pc-example.schema.json` are educational fixture contracts, not runtime DTOs; `semantic-execution-trace.schema.json` is a draft contract under proposed ADR-0071, bound at F0036/F0038 Phase B\n- `security/policies/` \u2014 Casbin model and policy; `security/` \u2014 AuthX contract and pending security artifacts\n- `testing/evaluation-strategy.md` \u2014 Golden Corpus, metrics, regression suites, release gates\n\n### 4.8 Open decisions\n\nSection 117.1 tracks the decisions for implementation and production acceptance: source-authority owner, tenant and knowledge-base identity scope, production host, licensed corpus and reviewers, acceptance thresholds and budgets, retention and deletion behavior. F0001 G1 (2026-09-06) answered the extension build (PostgreSQL 18) and the proof model policy (self-hosted), and ADR-0057 (2026-09-08) settled the review surface. F0005 closed on its rejection branch and ADR-0060 was Rejected on 2026-11-08. The current status of every item is in master blueprint section 117.1 (updated 2026-11-08).\n\n**Time-interpretation dependency for v0.1 (2026-09-25, validate finding P-1):** F0019 and F0025 take endorsement valid time from the template route's typed effective-date field. F0016 stores time mentions and document time context alongside. Resolution from time mentions (ADR-0064, Proposed) replaces the template field only after ADR-0064 passes its proof gates, which F0026 qualifies. v0.1 acceptance does not depend on a Proposed ADR.\n\n**Document-date candidate producer (opened 2026-10-16, F0004 plan-review M-1).** F0004 delivers the append-only document-date service but no runtime caller. No feature yet owns creating CONTENT or SOURCE_METADATA date candidates. F0022 owns the verified human selection decision, which in v0.1 is the only way to select or clear a date. Operator decision (2026-10-23, F0005 plan G1): F0016 owns producing both CONTENT and SOURCE_METADATA candidates; F0005 produces none. Until F0016 delivers, consumers see every document as undated, and F0019/F0025 continue to use the template route's typed effective-date field.\n\n**Retraction versus the information-state guard (opened 2026-11-21, drift review; owner F0010 G1).** The ADR-0078 D8 guard enforces the F0008 G1 operator rule that a `PRESENT` answer closes only to `PRESENT` or `EXPLICIT_NEGATIVE`. It is applied regardless of change reason (`brain_temporal/commit.py`, `_guard`). That protects against a silent later document erasing a known value. It also refuses a reviewed retraction of an erroneous extraction to `NOT_STATED`/`NOT_FOUND`, which section 16 (`RETRACTED_AS_ERRONEOUS_EXTRACTION`) requires.\n\n- **Recommendation (option A):** keep the guard for `SUPERSEDED`. Permit `PRESENT` \u2192 `NOT_STATED`/`NOT_FOUND` only for `CORRECTED`/`RETRACTED` commits that carry a review decision (ADR-0044 reviewer authority) and replace the same valid range, so the change is recorded-time only.\n- **Rejected alternatives:** closing with no successor, which would make reads return a false `NOT_PROCESSED` and breaks the ADR-0078 D5 insert; and using `EXPLICIT_NEGATIVE`, which fabricates a source statement.\n- **Next step:** F0010 decides at plan G1 and records the result as an ADR-0078 D8 amendment, with a reason-aware guard and tests for each reason \u00d7 state pair. No current caller commits retractions, so nothing is blocked before F0010.\n\n**F0065 assessment inputs versus the shipped F0007/F0008 contracts (opened 2026-11-21, drift review; owner F0065 targeted plan rework).** F0065's approved plan (2026-10-29) predates ADR-0077/0078. Its [assessment contract](features/F0065-grounded-gl-guideline-assessment/assessment-contract.md) is conceptually compatible (missing is `UNKNOWN`, explicit negative is `NOT_APPLICABLE`) but needs three bindings:\n\n1. Map the `fact-answer/v1` states: `PRESENT` is compared, `EXPLICIT_NEGATIVE` gives `NOT_APPLICABLE`, and every other state gives `UNKNOWN` with the state as reason. ADR-0078 D9 validity-unknown reads also give `UNKNOWN`.\n2. Take valid-time precision from the ADR-0078 D2 per-bound granularity columns, not from the Proposed ADR-0064.\n3. Replace the assumption that a grade-C mention carries no valid time. Under ADR-0078 a `MENTION_C` basis has bounds but cannot close a predecessor, so treat it as `valid_time_imprecise`.\n\nFold these into the already scheduled targeted rework for plan-review H1\u2013H3 (with F0018/F0020 Phase B). One `plan` run with `FEATURE_MODE=existing` re-approves the contract and S0002/S0004.\n\n**Account identity and account scope (opened 2026-10-09, direction set 2026-10-10).** The Cedar Bridge review asked whether Account is a party or a grouping of organizations, what an account-scoped grant reaches, what roots Entity 360, and how account identity relates to organization identity. The operator answered from commercial P&C practice, recorded in [ADR-0070](architecture/decisions/ADR-0070-account-party-and-role-model.md) (Proposed):\n\n- each insured organization has its own account, with at most one designated parent account; ownership between organizations is a separate relationship with any number of percentage owners (F0012);\n- a policy belongs to exactly one account, normally the first named insured's; other named insureds stay roles on the term, and a program's master and local policies link to the program, which belongs to the parent account (F0012, F0023);\n- brokers are organizations with hierarchy, locations and people; each account has a dated broker of record and broker contacts, and a policy term can name a different placement broker;\n- external people reach only what their authoritative roles name: an account and its own policies, or a single policy, never the parent's, a sibling's or the account behind a policy; carrier staff can see the tenant but act only where they hold the role. This needs an F0002-successor scope amendment to ADR-0062;\n- account identity and organization identity resolve separately (F0017).\n\nADR-0070 lists its proof gates; until it is accepted, F0012/F0013 Phase B plan against it.\n\n**Local proof decisions from F0001-S0007, updated for ADR-0060 (2026-09-15):**\n\n- **Item 3 (target host, PostgreSQL/extension build, model/provider data policy) \u2014 answered for the local proof scope.** The exact PostgreSQL/pgvector/AGE build is pinned and twice-verified live (S0002, re-verified at S0006 with no drift beyond an upstream base-image patch bump \u2014 `docker/DEPENDENCY-MATRIX.md`). The model/provider data policy is proven: self-hosted vLLM, chunk-text-only requests, no prompt persistence (F0001-S0003/S0006 live runs). The **production host** (as opposed to local Docker Compose) remains explicitly open, owned by F0026 per this feature's own G1 clarification and the F0001-S0006 story's stated assumption (\"the production host decision waits for F0026\").\n- **Item 4 (exact Docling-Graph implementation and release/commit) \u2014 closed.** Docling-Graph 1.9.1 / Docling 2.126.0 were locked and proved for the synthetic development scope ([F0005 compatibility evidence](features/archive/F0005-one-time-docling-ingestion/compatibility-evidence.md)). Graph dense then failed live qualification (F0005 run `2026-10-25-4020923b`, 2026-10-27), and the operator rejected ADR-0060 on 2026-11-08. The ADR-0074 execution controls ship for the direct-baseline pipeline.\n\n### 4.9 F0001 Phase B (2026-09-06)\n\nAssembly plan: `features/archive/F0001-repository-and-engineering-foundation/feature-assembly-plan.md` (eight steps). New decisions: ADR-0054 (runtime roots and local topology) and ADR-0055 (Phi-4-mini-instruct on vLLM). Contracts authored: `api/brain-api.yaml`, six schemas, Casbin model and policy for the proof roles TenantMember, Reviewer, ServicePrincipal. Knowledge graph: ten capabilities, ten entities, three workflows, six endpoints, three roles, five policy rules bound to F0001; code bindings follow at feature G7.\n\n---\n\n### 4.10 F0002 Phase B design (2026-09-25; design approved; implemented 2026-09-28)\n\n[Assembly plan](features/archive/F0002-tenancy-aware-domain-kernel-and-principal-contracts/feature-assembly-plan.md): structural Tenant/Workspace/KB ownership, tenant-scoped entity identity with explicit KB grants, stable verified principal aliases, complete current grant slices, conjunctive resource restrictions, bounded delegation and durable decision audit. User confirmed the entity/KB identity choice and reuse of the three existing pilot roles, then approved Phase A with `approve-phase-a` and Phase B with `approve-phase-b`. This resolves section 117.1 item 2 for the F0002 pilot scope; broader production rollout remains open.\n\nADR-0061/0062 (accepted 2026-09-28 for the bounded F0002 scope after feature run `2026-09-27-bb7c8d1d`; originally Proposed), AuthX v1 schema and OpenAPI design version 0.2.0 specify compatible migrations and existing-consumer integration. No new runtime or policy grants are delivered. F0002 proves review and canonical commit authorization independently; F0018 owns full review-to-canonical orchestration and F0022 owns review UI. This explicitly reconciles the old master-blueprint \u00a7116.1 F0002 wiring shorthand without broadening the approved PRD. Existing C4 deployment topology is unchanged; the feature README adds its ERD and component diagram. ADR-0042/0052/0053 remain Proposed for broader obligations.\n\n### 4.11 Statements, time, and governance amendments (2026-09-25)\n\nThe operator reviewed Utopia's decisions made after this repository started (2026-09-05, Utopia commit `b3919ca`) and approved incorporating them.\n\n- **[ADR-0063](architecture/decisions/ADR-0063-open-statements-and-signature-alignment.md), accepted as direction.** Open statements in the source's own words, beside typed assertions. Typed assertions come from template extraction (form-shaped sections) or from per-signature alignment (narrative sections, F0066, v0.2B).\n- **[ADR-0064](architecture/decisions/ADR-0064-time-interpretation-and-valid-time-precision.md) to [ADR-0069](architecture/decisions/ADR-0069-action-attempts-and-uncertain-outcomes.md), Proposed.** They cover time interpretation and valid-time precision, assertion admission, text origin and mood, names as time-bounded claims, impact-gated automation with human precedent and a revert fuse, decision basis fingerprints, and external action attempts.\n\n**v0.1 impact** is limited to storage and contracts, because they are expensive to retrofit after F0003, F0006, and F0008 ship:\n\n- F0004 (document date source, text origin);\n- F0006 (assertion kinds, admission, mood);\n- F0007 and F0013 (name FactSlots, temporal kinds);\n- F0008 (precision, unknown ends);\n- F0014 (interpretation route);\n- F0016 (time mentions, drops, basis);\n- F0017 (identifier-first names);\n- F0019, F0022, F0025, F0026.\n\nv0.1 acceptance still runs on the template route. Later features carry the behavioural parts: F0027, F0032, F0043, F0050, F0052, F0056, F0059.\n\n**v0.1 scope guard (validate finding P-2).** Each v0.1 feature's Phase A admits only the storage fields, contract checks, and review/display hooks named in its amendment. It does not admit:\n\n- alignment execution;\n- automated deciders;\n- fingerprint-driven scheduling;\n- time-mention resolution replacing template fields;\n- action dispatch.\n\nAnything beyond this guard needs a new operator scope amendment.\n\nScope amendments are recorded in each feature README. Master blueprint sections 3, 11, 14, 17, 29, 53, 56, 62, 64, 75, 76, 78, 95, and 99 were revised in place, and the glossary and [examples EX-SEM-001\u2013011](examples/statements-time-and-governance.md) were added.\n\n**Not changed:** F0002's approved plan. Utopia's same-knowledge-base provenance record (0048) matches F0002's composite ownership keys. Its extra safeguards were left as a follow-up for the F0002 implementation run, and the operator brought them into that run at its G4 approval gate (2026-09-28, scope amendment recorded in run `2026-09-27-bb7c8d1d` gate-decisions.md). Engine migration 0007 implements them:\n\n- ownership columns made immutable by trigger (plus the principal links of memberships, identity aliases and delegations), with append-only `audit_event` and `authentication_event`;\n- link tables without an owner column (`outbox_event`, `document_job_event`) have a single parent whose foreign key fixes their ownership, and every multi-parent link table carries owner columns with composite keys since 0006, so no separate link trigger is needed;\n- deferrable (initially immediate) self-references on the assertion correction chain for restore.\n\n---\n\n### 4.12 F0006 assertion contracts and guards (implemented; archived 2026-11-05)\n\n[Assembly plan](features/archive/F0006-assertion-plane-origin-and-interpretation-basis/feature-assembly-plan.md), plan run `2026-11-01-7d6d19ce`: Phase A and Phase B approved by operator tokens `approve-phase-a` and `approve-phase-b`; five stories and 35 ACs, now implemented in feature run `2026-11-02-5a00b0ff`. Proposed [ADR-0075](architecture/decisions/ADR-0075-versioned-assertion-semantics-and-admission.md) defines additive typed/open assertion semantics, document-local references/name admission claims, structural quote/name/time checks and eligibility guards at existing review/commit consumers. The legacy strict result contract and source history remain; new schemas are `assertion-record-v2`, `interpretation-result-v2` and `assertion-admission-result-v1`. Case/spacing normalization is deterministic with original-range mapping; repeated text never justifies a fabricated span.\n\nNo new deployable, assertion HTTP route, UI, grants or extraction activation. Current authorization's mutation facade gains optional source READ requirements in the same unit of work; it must not nest a read facade that commits the outer transaction. Existing `direct-baseline` and v1 content writer defaults follow F0005's final approved rejection decision. Full durable drops/run adoption stays F0016; full source-completeness/commit orchestration stays F0018; display stays F0022; open extraction/alignment stays F0066. New restrictions apply to attributable v2 evidence/review/correction lineage; unregistered legacy pilot references remain an explicit compatibility boundary. ADR-0065 and ADR-0075 remain Proposed until their required runtime proofs. Existing C4 topology is unchanged; feature README contains ER/component diagrams. Bounded implementation is complete: 336 unique final product cases pass and changed executable-line coverage is 1170/1266 (92.4171%). The operator approved SEC-01 only for trusted local synthetic fixtures; dependencies and resource isolation must be remediated/qualified before untrusted or production PDFs (AI Engineer + DevOps; Security verification; target 2026-11-10). Broader ADR proof/activation gates remain separate. Evidence: [PM closeout](operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-02-5a00b0ff/pm-closeout.md).\n\n---\n\n### 4.13 Governed retrieval and spectral planning amendment (2026-11-06)\n\nThe operator requested incorporation of the [handoff](architecture/nebula-spectral-graph-intelligence-handoff.md) across planning. [Master blueprint section 127](architecture/master-blueprint.md#127-governed-evidence-retrieval-and-spectral-graph-inspiration) names SpectRAG as an inspiration and distinguishes its official implementation from the independent SpectraFuse reference. [Integrated design](architecture/governed-evidence-retrieval-design.md) and [ADR-0076](architecture/decisions/ADR-0076-governed-graph-assisted-evidence-retrieval.md) (Proposed) define the derived retrieval boundary.\n\n- F0033/F0034 carry versioned persisted-content and typed projection/checkpoint requirements; settle their contracts before F0035 Phase B approval.\n- F0035/F0036 carry authorized hybrid seeds, bounded expansion, optional PPR, exact model-budgeted evidence sets, locator/current-authority revalidation, gaps and answer-basis traces at v0.2A. Source/canonical modes, bitemporality and current grants remain controlling contracts.\n- F0067 consumes recorded diagnostics later at v0.2B; baseline trace recording has no rendering dependency.\n- Reserve F0068 for conditional spectral/heat experiments at v0.4+ (D3 recommended separate home). F0061 retains its advanced retrieval scope. Baseline measurement and a separate experiment scope/scheduling/cost decision precede spectral implementation or activation.\n\nPM owns requirements and sequencing; Architect owns design, ADR and structural KG relationships; Security owns authorization/cache/replay review; AI Engineer and QE own model/numerical proposals and evaluation with PM. Numbered RET inputs are in the feature READMEs, with [worked examples](examples/governed-evidence-retrieval.md), [evaluation](testing/evaluation-strategy.md#governed-retrieval-and-spectral-experiment-evaluation) and [security](security/authorization-review.md#governed-retrieval-carry-in-2026-11-06) coverage. D4\u2013D9 remain scoped Phase A/B decisions. This is a roadmap/design incorporation, not a completed per-feature plan, approval or implementation; all affected features remain Planned.\n\n---\n\n### 4.14 F0007 FactSlot identity and answer carriers (Phase B approved 2026-11-09; review remediation completed 2026-11-10)\n\nPlan run `2026-11-09-60865e32`: Phase A and Phase B were approved on 2026-11-09 with operator tokens `approve-phase-a` and `approve-phase-b`. The [assembly plan](features/archive/F0007-factslot-model/feature-assembly-plan.md) and [ADR-0077](architecture/decisions/ADR-0077-factslot-identity-and-typed-answer-carriers.md) define the design.\n\n- **Slot identity:** tenant, KB, subject, an opaque major-versioned predicate key and normalized qualifier rows, with a versioned SHA-256/JCS fingerprint used only for lookup. Concurrent resolvers converge on one slot. A collision is rejected, never merged.\n- **Members:** MULTI members are child slot rows, so the ADR-0008 exclusion applies per member without changing the F0008-owned version table.\n- **Answers:** the `fact-answer/v1` envelope carries the nine information states, scoped absence, exact money in its original currency, and scheme-scoped identifiers. It is validated at the existing commit for identity-v1 slots only.\n- **Names:** the four ADR-0066 name predicates are F0007 system predicates. The display hook applies no precedence.\n- **Authorization:** slot creation derives restrictions from its source artifacts under the existing `content_artifact:interpret` authority. F0007 adds no grants, routes or UI.\n- **Legacy pilot slots:** they stay legacy, with no fabricated identity.\n- **Row-level security:** the inventory (`fact_slot`, `fact_slot_qualifier`) is handed to F0018.\n\nThe design schemas are `fact-slot-key-v1`, `fact-answer-v1` and `fact-slot-resolution-result-v1`. The C4 topology is unchanged, and the feature README carries the ER and component views.\n\nFeature run `2026-11-09-b94cfa12` implemented the design: domain modules in `brain_domain`, the `brain-factslots` package, migration 0012 and the commit/read hooks. The run proved all 39 ACs and the five ADR-0077 proof gates against PostgreSQL. The G3 security review fixed three access-control gaps:\n\n- name evidence is READ-checked before any reason;\n- T-08 now holds on the answer read path;\n- a foreign evidence assertion is indistinguishable from a missing one.\n\nADR-0077 was accepted by the operator on 2026-11-10; ADR-0039 and ADR-0066 stay Proposed.\n\n---\n\n### 4.15 F0008 bitemporal version contract (Phase B approved 2026-11-17; implemented and archived 2026-11-18)\n\nPlan run `2026-11-16-208a1193`. The [assembly plan](features/archive/F0008-bitemporal-canonical-facts/feature-assembly-plan.md) and [ADR-0078](architecture/decisions/ADR-0078-bitemporal-version-contract-and-close-only-immutability.md) (Accepted 2026-11-19) define the design:\n\n- **Precision and zone:** each valid-time bound stores a granularity and an IANA zone. Truncation is checked in the service and authoritatively in a database trigger. The caller applies document conventions.\n- **Ends and attestation:** `OPEN`, `BOUNDED` or `UNKNOWN`. An unknown end closes the integrity range at the end of its `attested_to` period (the ADR-0064 option). The attestation dates come from F0004 date selections, never from clocks. An unknown start is floored at `attested_from`, or refused when no evidence is dated.\n- **Immutability:** closing an open recorded interval is the only permitted update. Triggers refuse every other UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE, and `canonical_fact_change` is append-only. Remainders keep their predecessor's payload, evidence and timestamps.\n- **Guards:** a grade-`C` or attestation-floor start closes nothing. A `PRESENT` value closes only to `PRESENT` or `EXPLICIT_NEGATIVE`. An end revision is not a succession.\n- **Reads:** an internal two-coordinate reader returns the version, validity-unknown or `NOT_PROCESSED`. The existing GET adds a `temporal` block and a validity-unknown 200 variant, and a coordinate with no version stays 404.\n- **Relationships:** RELATIONSHIP slots are versioned in the same table, and no separate relationship-version table is created.\n\nNo new route, grant, table or UI is added. Migration 0014 is additive with a guarded downgrade. ADR-0064 and ADR-0039 remain Proposed.\n\nFeature run `2026-11-17-1a4ae2f0` implemented the design and was approved by the operator at G4 on 2026-11-18. It delivers migration 0014, `brain_domain.temporal`, `brain_temporal` bounds/attestation/commit/reader and the additive `/facts` changes. All 46 ACs and the six ADR-0078 proof gates pass on PostgreSQL 18 (1081 engine tests; 98.0% changed-line coverage). The operator accepted ADR-0078 on 2026-11-19 (decision run `2026-11-19-12422004`). SEC-F8-02 (the application connects as a superuser) and refusal reason persistence move to F0018. Independent review `2026-11-18-d34a095e` returned NOT DONE. Remediation run `2026-11-18-bce4909b` (approved 2026-11-19) added the commit-response temporal metadata, the legacy read shape and migration 0015 (same-slot lineage), amended S0004 AC1 and S0007 AC6, and recorded the F0018 handoffs. A second review, `2026-11-19-b21ec2de`, found that the new commit response could return a predecessor's attestation dates without READ on their documents (SEC-F8-NEW-01, High). Second remediation run `2026-11-19-8cfcd0ff` (approved 2026-11-19) refuses the whole commit with the non-disclosing 404 in that case. Evidence: [PM closeout](operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-19-8cfcd0ff/pm-closeout.md).\n\n---\n\n### 4.16 F0011 JSON Schema contract system (Done / Archived 2026-11-23)\n\nPlan run `2026-11-20-ccb1bd39`: Phase A approved by operator response `approve`;\nsix stories and 41 ACs. Implemented and closed in feature run `2026-11-22-885e8734` (G0\u2013G8, operator\nG4 approval 2026-11-23); all six stories Done. The [assembly plan](features/archive/F0011-json-schema-contract-system/feature-assembly-plan.md)\nand proposed [ADR-0079](architecture/decisions/ADR-0079-offline-schema-bundle-and-cross-language-conformance.md)\ndefine one authored JSON Schema 2020-12 source, a generated root runtime snapshot\nand installed offline bundle, source-gated generated Pydantic, headless AJV and\nshared metadata/OpenAPI. The inventory has 21 payload resources; additive value\naliases reference the shipped definitions. Existing readers retain explicit\nnative compatibility and current authority/domain guard ordering. A fact-read\nschema reconciles the stale nested OpenAPI description to the already shipped\nflat timestamps. As built, the read and commit routes validate their normalized responses\nafter authorization (commit inside the mutation, so a failure rolls back), and the 500\nhandlers log a correlatable traceId.\n\nNo new registry table, migration, route, grant, deployable, screen or reparse is\nrequired. ADR-0079 and ADR-0039 remain Proposed pending their stated proofs.\nG4 ontology synchronization and all ordered G5 pre-approval exit checks passed.\nThe operator approved Phase B with `approve-phase-b` on 2026-11-20; G5 performs\npost-approval regeneration/validation and publishes the manifest last. Independent\nplan-review `2026-11-21-b4cd07e4` returned READY for that baseline. Phase B revision\n`2026-11-21-e4098d22` was approved by operator token `approve-phase-b` on\n2026-11-22; its G5 journal/manifest records post-approval checks and publication.\nThe revision adds per-resource consumer mappings,\nread-only integration/dev full-history response-guard preflight, and PR-L3\nSecurity follow-up due at feature G3. Existing C4 topology is unchanged.\n\n### 4.17 Delivery reconciliation (2026-11-21)\n\nA drift review compared the planning artifacts with the code delivered through F0008 (migrations 0001\u20130015). It reconciled the master blueprint (sections 13, 14, 76, 77, 78, 95.1, 106.3, 109, 116.1), `architecture/data-model.md` and `architecture/c4-container.md`. Three features had no Phase B summary here:\n\n- **F0003** (feature run `2026-10-03-57d14a51`): recorded the persistence ownership and phase boundaries over migrations 0001\u20130007. No schema change.\n- **F0004** ([assembly plan](features/archive/F0004-content-artifact-model/feature-assembly-plan.md)): migration 0008 adds version-aware artifact metadata, normalized block/table/cell indexes with `text_origin`, artifact state events, repair records, and append-only document-date candidates/selections. ADR-0073 remains Proposed.\n- **F0005** ([compatibility evidence](features/archive/F0005-one-time-docling-ingestion/compatibility-evidence.md)): closed on its rejection branch. Fenced document jobs (migration 0004, reasons in 0009\u20130010) run under the accepted ADR-0074 controls. The direct-baseline client is the v0.1 extraction path.\n\nEvery recipient of the ADR-0077/ADR-0078 handoffs (F0009, F0010, F0012, F0013, F0016\u2013F0020, F0022, F0023, F0025, F0026, F0065, F0069) carries a \"Shipped contract carry-in\" note in its README. F0011's plan already binds them. Their Phase B binds to the as-built contract, not to the original section 13/14 sketch.\n\n---\n\n### 4.18 F0009 provenance and correction lineage (Phase B approved 2026-11-24; implemented and archived 2026-11-25)\n\nPlan run `2026-11-24-bfdbbf04`; Phase A explicitly approved by operator token `approve-phase-a`, six stories and 41 ACs (all Done 2026-11-25). The [assembly plan](features/archive/F0009-provenance-and-human-correction-lineage/feature-assembly-plan.md) and proposed [ADR-0080](architecture/decisions/ADR-0080-bounded-provenance-and-correction-reservations.md) define an internal metadata-first reader over exact assertion/version lineage, current READ of every linked source/review/ending/attestation resource, two append-only tables for future-learning reservations and non-applied submission attribution, and a nullable server-owned new-decision marker. Legacy rows are not backfilled; canonical writes remain with the shipped commit service and full orchestration remains F0018.\n\nThe four design schemas use F0011 delivery in the later feature action; no runtime bundle, route, grant, UI, deployable, parse or learning producer is added by plan. A losing batch keeps its existing 422 after protected audit-only persistence, and a new effective CORRECT receives one reference atomically. G4 and all seven ordered G5 pre-approval checks passed; the operator approved Phase B with exact token `approve-phase-b` on 2026-11-24. The same run\u2019s G5 journal/manifest records post-approval regeneration, checks and final publication. ADR-0080 is Proposed until its runtime proofs and separate acceptance.\n\nFeature run `2026-11-24-08701e37` implemented the design, with operator G4 approval on 2026-11-25. It delivers `brain_domain.provenance`, the `brain-provenance` reader (exported, not routed), the opt-in `prepare_reads` authorization hook, review-boundary preflight with refused-attempt attribution and an atomic learning reservation, and migration 0016. All 41 ACs and EX-PROV-001\u2013005 are proven on PostgreSQL 18 (changed-line coverage 94.4%; 1392/1392 shared conformance results). G2 recorded five design corrections, among them a nullable `fact_change.from_version_id` and attempt authorization bound by `audit_event.decision_id` (see the run reports). ADR-0080 runtime proofs are met; the ADR stays Proposed pending operator acceptance. Evidence: [PM closeout](operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-24-08701e37/pm-closeout.md). F0010 owns retraction semantics; F0020/F0022/F0023 own exposure and F0041/F0026 own learning/benchmark governance.\n\n\n### 4.19 F0012 foundation ontology (Phase B approved 2026-11-25; implemented and archived 2026-11-26)\n\nPlan run `2026-11-25-120320e9`; Phase A approved by operator token `approve-phase-a` (seven stories, 46 ACs; G1 decisions D1\u2013D8). The [assembly plan](features/archive/F0012-foundation-ontology/feature-assembly-plan.md) and proposed [ADR-0081](architecture/decisions/ADR-0081-foundation-ontology-authoring-and-release-runtime.md) define: YAML modules under `ontology/` validated by `ontology-module-authoring/v1` (`parents:` only; inference `subClassOf`/`subPropertyOf`/`inverseOf`; validation-only domain/range/disjoint/cardinality with execution context; other constructs refused); `urn:nebula:ont:` IRIs with reuse/collision refusal and change records; a deterministic compiler producing content-addressed releases (`ontrel:sha256-\u2026`) with exact locks, projection mapping and RDF/JSON-LD export; migration 0017 with eight append-only, tenant/KB-owned release tables; a release-backed predicate registry (`fnd` namespace, 15 foundation predicates) and ETERNAL/EVENT activation over the ADR-0078 D10 shapes without DDL; an impact report and reviewed, audited activation/rollback under a new `ontology_release` resource and `OntologySteward` role. The foundation module carries the section 22 classes and the ADR-0070 party/account/ownership/role vocabulary; Policy/Submission/Program stay with F0013. Canonical-admission constraints are declared for F0017/F0018. No HTTP route, screen, parse or model call. ADR-0045/0070/0081 remain Proposed. The operator approved Phase B with `approve-phase-b` on 2026-11-25. As built (feature run `2026-11-26-54387a08`, archived 2026-11-26; no plan-review ran, and the operator chose G0 reconciliation): foundation@1 is committed under `ontology/releases/foundation/1` (`ontrel:sha256-3602b71f\u2026`). The `ontology_release` authorization resource is the KB's ontology scope with a required trusted `resource_access` row, and migration 0017 widens `ck_resource_access_type`. `fact-version-read-v1` `valid_start` is nullable for ETERNAL versions. RDF exports domain/range as `nebula:validationDomain`/`validationRange`. Reports require the steward's `review` grant.\n\n### 4.20 F0021 native React shell and BFF session (Phase B approved 2026-11-27)\n\nPlan run `2026-11-27-6cda122a`. Phase A was approved on 2026-11-27 with nine stories and 55 ACs. G1 decisions:\n\n- D1: 30-minute idle and 8-hour absolute session limits;\n- D2: the shell includes the rehosted Review Panel;\n- D3: re-authentication in a popup, with explicit re-confirmation of blocked actions;\n- D4: 20 rejected credentials per client per 60 seconds, then 429.\n\nThe [assembly plan](features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/feature-assembly-plan.md) and proposed [ADR-0082](architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md) fix the runtime choices that ADR-0051 leaves to F0021:\n\n- **BFF placement and origin:** the BFF runs inside the engine API process. One public origin serves the shell at `/` and the engine under a stripped `/api` mount; contract paths stay at the root.\n- **Identity client:** the authentik `brain` client becomes confidential, keeping the same issuer, audience and principals.\n- **Session store:** migration 0018 adds:\n  - `browser_login_attempt`;\n  - `browser_session`, with AES-256-GCM token ciphertext under a key ring;\n  - append-only `session_event`;\n  - `credential_rejection_window`;\n  - nullable tenant and knowledge-base display names.\n- **Cookies:** `__Host-nebula_session` and `__Host-nebula_login` are 256-bit, `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`.\n- **CSRF:** a synchronizer token from `GET /session`, plus `Origin`, `Referer` and `Sec-Fetch-Site` checks. Sending both a cookie and a bearer token is refused.\n- **Renewal:** one upstream refresh per burst, coalesced by a PostgreSQL row lock (60-second margin, one bounded retry).\n- **Logout:** RFC 7009 revocation with a truthful outcome, and an end-session URL without `id_token_hint`.\n- **Re-authentication and other tabs:** the popup signals completion over BroadcastChannel and `postMessage`. Tabs learn about sign-out through BroadcastChannel and a 30-second background session poll.\n- **Throttle:** an atomic per-client window counter in PostgreSQL, bounded at 21 events per window.\n- **Session endpoint:** `browser-session-v1` carries memberships, an opaque `grant_revision`, the active knowledge base and server-side flags. The active knowledge base never authorizes anything.\n- **Return routes:** a server-side allowlist.\n- **Shell:** the section 2.1 stack. It has a route, flag and lazy-loading registry with a 180 kB gzip entry-chunk budget, one API client, and hygiene triggers.\n- **Real-browser proof:** Playwright with a test-only IdP recorder that counts refresh grants and injects revocation failures.\n\nThe operator approved Phase B with `approve-phase-b` on 2026-11-27, confirming reconciliations R1 and R2 (wording fixes to two Phase A ACs, made by the PM at feature G0):\n\n- R1: engine denials stay the non-disclosing 404;\n- R2: verification stays local while a client is throttled.\n\nADR-0051 and ADR-0082 remain Proposed until S0009 passes.\n\n---\n\n## 5) Phase C \u2014 Implementation Plan (locked order)\n\nSequence per master blueprint sections 115.3 and 124; original identifiers F0001 to F0063 are preserved. F0065 is the bounded v0.1 assessment addition; F0064 is repository tooling.\n\n1. Archived F0001 supplies the measured foundation contracts. Archived F0005 supplies the checkpoint/reuse, recovery and execution-control proof (ADR-0074); its Docling-Graph candidate was rejected (ADR-0060 Rejected 2026-11-08; sections 115.4, 126).\n2. v0.1A \u2014 F0002 to F0017: typed domain contracts, durable ingestion, immutable evidence, assertion extraction\n3. v0.1B \u2014 F0018 to F0023 establish authorized commits, temporal reads, evidence review, and minimal 360 views; F0065 adds bounded on-demand GL guideline assessment; F0024/F0025 prove real interpretation-to-assessment and temporal reassessment end to end\n4. v0.1C \u2014 F0069 (constrained policy question, added 2026-11-08) then F0026: recovery, deletion and revocation minimum, audit, independent frozen evaluation, constrained policy question, and F0065 assessment/lineage/freshness/access challenge cases\n5. v0.2A \u2014 F0033 to F0040 and F0044 to F0047; v0.2B \u2014 F0027 to F0032, F0066 (open-statement alignment, ADR-0063), F0041 to F0043, and F0067 (Graph Observatory, ADR-0071/ADR-0072)\n6. v0.3 and later \u2014 F0048 to F0063: full process, generalized reasoning, automatic derivation propagation, decision replay, and advanced semantics; F0065 is already in v0.1B\n7. v0.4+ conditional \u2014 F0068 spectral graph retrieval experiments, only after the F0035/F0036 baseline is measured and its own experiment scope/scheduling/cost decision is recorded. Baseline delivery does not depend on this branch.\n\nBaseline authenticated writes, approval checks, source restrictions, and audit are v0.1 obligations even though the full Execution Gate and Decision Ledger come later (section 89).\n\n---\n\n## 6) Next Step Guidance\n\nCurrent position (2026-11-20): F0001 to F0008 are done and archived; ADR-0078 was accepted on 2026-11-19 (F0008 second remediation run `2026-11-19-8cfcd0ff`, approved 2026-11-19). F0007 review remediation completed in approved run `2026-11-09-81798e61`: all seven findings resolved, fresh868 engine/27 Neuron tests and current independent reviews pass. Prior completion remains superseded history; ADR-0077 accepted 2026-11-10; remediation merged as PR #44. No production rollout or new ontology/producer/permission scope.\n\n1. Now (2026-11-20 roadmap review, after F0008 closed): four lanes.\n   - **F0011** (JSON Schema contract system) completed 2026-11-23 in feature run `2026-11-22-885e8734` (no migration added).\n   - **F0009** (provenance + human-correction lineage) completed 2026-11-25 in feature run `2026-11-24-08701e37` (migration 0016); F0010 \u2192 F0018 continue the temporal/commit path.\n   - **F0012** (foundation ontology) completed 2026-11-26 in feature run `2026-11-26-54387a08` (migration 0017); F0013 composes its GL modules on foundation@1.\n   - **F0021** (React shell + OIDC/session) takes the Now slot freed by F0008, as the 2026-11-10 review promised.\n\n   Next is reordered by dependency readiness: F0010, F0013, F0014, F0017, F0015, F0016. Each lane runs `plan-review` before its feature action.\n2. Carry ADR-0070 (account, party and role model, Proposed) into F0012/F0013 Phase B. The operator aligns the data contracts and CRM separately, following the [cross-repository plan](architecture/account-model-cross-repo-plan.md).\n3. F0012 is done (2026-11-26); F0013 plans against the shipped foundation release, as described in the [ontology planning handoff](architecture/ontology-planning-handoff.md) and the [commercial P&C handoff](architecture/commercial-pc-example-handoff.md).\n4. Once per clone: `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`, and `pip install -e '.[test,semantic-rdf]'` so the `semantic_rdf` gate runs instead of skipping.\n\n\n### F0007 review remediation\n\nF0007 remediation is complete and archived in run `2026-11-09-81798e61`, with explicit operator G4 approval. All seven independent findings were resolved and revalidated; original completion/audits remain historical. No new route, producer, permission or formal ADR acceptance.\n"
